## Decisions Made

- **Single-approved is a WRITE-side invariant** (Director's correction): never "newest-of-many" read logic; approving one demotes siblings → INVALIDATED at approve-time + DB unique index. (q24 = INVALIDATED, not REJECTED — keeps rollback, no re-gen trigger.)
- **q25:** auto-bounce loop ON in Mode 1 (REVISE→author→cap=2→HALT→Director), generalized to all plan critics. (Build in Phase 2.)
- **Two-layer plan** = my structural audit (money/integrity) MERGED with the "caveman" process material (auto-bounce, OUTPUT-critic, media-preflight). The caveman material caught OUTPUT-critic + auto-bounce that I'd underweighted; it MISSED the money landmines my hunters found.
- **Build order:** Phase1(money+garbage) → Phase2(process) → Phase3(output).
- **Don't invent entities; minimal changes** (Director rule, saved to memory) — the whole fix is CONSOLIDATION (one resolver, one paid path, one demote helper) + REUSE (DB index pattern, capability model), not new sprawl.

